'[ ]' pre-hash; only item-TEXT edits invalidate), (2) AC-checkbox completeness precheck section notes box-checking is attestation-safe via the single 330c seam shared with the completion-verifier staleness check. AC3 grep swept docs/: no other live doc claims box flips stale a review (user-guide silent; ADR 0002 is code-drift only; experiments/research corpora are historical records, not guidance). Pushed as Gerrit change 1349 (Change-Id Ibef002bd, commit e124186458). Awaiting LLM-Review + Verified.","timestamp":1785821182630576001}],"created_at":1785806357220450001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7974b1aa-9b64-4729-8483-107edd0e21ac","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"330c-1c85-5bd4-48b5"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nChange 330c (commit 9ba1e90e3c, \"box flips no longer stale attestations\") normalizes AC checkbox STATE (case-insensitive x, - or * bullets, line-anchored) to '[ ]' before hashing the material fingerprint, so flipping boxes at close no longer stales a plan-review attestation or the completion-verifier staleness check. The commit touched only src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py + tests — no documentation.\n\ndocs/plan-review-gate.md still teaches the OLD behavior:\n\n- §\"Attestation, freshness & invalidation\" (~L469): \"the bound material fingerprint matches the current ticket — a material edit (description/AC/file-impact/decomposition) invalidates it. (Tags/comments/links/assignee are not material and do not invalidate.)\" — a reader concludes any description edit, including box flips, invalidates. Checkbox-state flips are now explicitly NOT material.\n- The close-gate flow describes the AC-checkbox completeness precheck (~L901) requiring boxes checked before close, with no note that checking them is fingerprint-safe — the exact author fear the 330c fix removed.\n\n## Plan\n\nUpdate docs/plan-review-gate.md:\n1. In the invalidation list (~L469), extend the non-material parenthetical: checkbox state ('- [ ]' vs '- [x]', either bullet, either case) is normalized out of the material fingerprint; flipping boxes never stales an attestation — only item TEXT edits do.\n2. In the AC-checkbox completeness precheck section (~L901), add one sentence: checking boxes to satisfy this precheck does not invalidate the plan-review attestation (330c normalization; single seam covers plan-review close gate and completion-verifier staleness).\n3. Grep docs/ for other statements that description edits invalidate attestations (completion-verifier docs, user-guide) and align them.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] docs/plan-review-gate.md invalidation rules state that checkbox-state flips are normalized out of the material fingerprint and only item-text edits invalidate.\n- [ ] The AC-checkbox completeness precheck section notes that satisfying it is attestation-safe.\n- [ ] No other doc still claims box flips stale a review (grep for material-edit invalidation statements across docs/).\n\n## File impact\n\n- docs/plan-review-gate.md (edit)\n- possibly docs/user-guide.md (edit, if it restates invalidation rules)","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"update invalidation rules + AC-precheck note for 330c checkbox normalization"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"align any restated invalidation rules"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e7337fe9-d147-443d-8d9d-e391e22aafcd","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"51c1-22cf-0908-44e6","ticket_type":"task","title":"Document checkbox-state normalization in attestation-staleness docs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["acc8fe0e-446d-4a91-957b-2b0c30d112b1","651c86b5-f716-4473-a533-f00af7d240cb","7974b1aa-9b64-4729-8483-10